        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0242" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/55.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 849.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Sir: I have the honor to inclose herewith the correspondence between this
                    legation and the Haitian Government relative to the negotiation by our
                    Government of a convention for arbitration of the frontier question between
                    Haiti and Santo Domingo.</p>
                <p>It is to be noted that the secretary of foreign relations states that the Haitian
                    Government will be pleased to send to its minister at Washington instructions to
                    request the American Government to negotiate the convention.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
